# Netlify reads this from the DEPLOYED directory, not from the clone, so it is copied into out/ by
# the build like any other asset. Nothing generates it: .htaccess carries no Header directive worth
# translating, so this whole file is the trunk.

# READABLE FROM ANYWHERE, and across the whole site rather than under one prefix.
#
# Two things need it. The (?) panel of each reconstruction hands out a self-contained markup snippet
# meant to be pasted into any other site: that page loads the module bundle AND the observation's own
# JSON cross-origin. And the case CATALOG (@rr0/case, which vraiufo.com is built on) reads
# /casesDirs.json at the root and then a case.json inside each of the 261 directories it names.
#
# Those directories are the reason this is not a prefix list. A case file lives NEXT TO THE PAGE IT
# DOCUMENTS — under science/ for most, but also people/ for a witness's own file and time/ for one
# dated 1608 — because that is how this site is arranged, and any new case may land anywhere in it.
# A list of prefixes would be a list that has to be kept in step with a directory tree deliberately
# left open, and it would fail silently the first time it fell out of step: exactly what happened
# once, where the catalog's own index sat at the root and outside the one prefix listed.
#
# Nothing is given away by it. Every one of these files is already public, served to anyone who asks
# over plain HTTP, with no session and no credentials anywhere near them — a browser refusing to hand
# a script bytes it will happily render is protecting nothing here.
/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
